+### Compound Format
+
+Use `compound` to format a number as multiple units, largest first. Only days, hours, minutes and seconds are used, zero parts are skipped, and any leftover milliseconds are dropped (so `500` becomes `"0s"`). Durations longer than a day are not rolled up into weeks, months or years. `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })             // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })            // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(3601000, { compound: true })             // "1h 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })            // "-1h 30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })                // "1s"
+```
+
